[h1]Stationeers UI Ascended 1.0[/h1]
[b]A UI overhaul that rebuilds Stationeers' inventory and HUD around your two hands.[/b] Radial wheels instead of menu-diving, a curved suit visor you can redesign live, and a Smart Stow that puts things back where they came from - all while keeping the game's own physical inventory rules.

[b]REQUIRES BepInEx 5 + StationeersLaunchPad.[/b] This is a StationeersLaunchPad plugin mod: install those first, then subscribe here and launch the game through StationeersLaunchPad.

[h2]Radial wheels[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Belt Wheel (middle mouse)[/b] - hold, flick and release to grab a tool; tap to leave it open and click. Every tool keeps its own wedge, and an empty slot shows a ghost of the tool that belongs there.
[*][b]Inventory wheel (Tab)[/b] - your worn bags plus Search: type to find anything you carry, however deep it is buried.
[*][b]Device wheel (R)[/b] - every setting vanilla shows for the item in your hand: jetpack thrust, suit pressure and temperature, visor, lights, tank valves. Scroll to adjust; hold C for fine steps.
[*][b]Gear keys 1-6[/b] - tap for that piece of gear's wheel (swap batteries, filters, canisters); hold to equip or unequip, like vanilla.
[*]The wheel names what a click will do (TAKE / EQUIP / SWAP / OPEN / STOW). Drag items out of any wheel onto a charger, into a locker or into a bag.
[/list]

[h2]Two hands. No hotbar. Ever.[/h2]
The bottom of your screen is exactly two hand boxes plus your worn gear (1-6), with live thumbnails and damage bars. The good friction - hands, batteries, real logistics - stays. The menu-diving goes.

[h2]Universal Inventory (B)[/h2]
[list]
[*]One window with every bag you carry, nested bags included. Tap B to toggle it, hold B to peek.
[*]Drag and drop to move, swap and merge. Pin any bag out into its own window.
[*]Shift+drag moves every stack of a type at once - into and out of lockers too.
[*]Drag straight into chargers, lockers and other world containers.
[*]Shift+1-6 jumps straight to that worn bag.
[/list]

[h2]Smart Stow (G) that remembers[/h2]
Every item remembers the exact bag and slot you last put it in, in each world, and G sends it back there - even into a belt inside a backpack. Move something by hand and its home moves with it. Prefer rules? Complex mode gives you Storage Layouts and Bag Profiles you can share with a code.

[h2]A curved visor HUD[/h2]
[list]
[*]Compass ribbon, status bar, a vitals card with a live hologram portrait, the game's real status moodlets and body damage.
[*]Diegetic: exact numbers need a powered suit - without one you get words like WARM, COLD and THIN AIR. The visor boots up, glitches as your suit battery runs down, and collapses when it dies.
[*]Four themes ship: Stationeers Blue, Stationeers Blue Minimalist, Zirillian Red and Pure HUD.
[/list]

[h2]F9 HUD Designer[/h2]
Click any part of the HUD to move, resize or restyle it live: frosted glass, glow, edge light, cut corners, your own labels and icons, and separate looks for suited and bare. Save it as your own theme and share it.

[h2]F10 Control Center[/h2]
Every setting in one place, with search. Rebind every key. Turn the radial half or the HUD half off independently.

[h2]Report bugs from inside the game[/h2]
F10 > Suggestions/Bugs: describe it, optionally attach your HUD layout or recent log lines, and it reaches the developers as a tracked report you can follow right in the menu. Anonymous unless you add a contact - your Steam ID and save name are never sent.

[h2]Learn it as you play[/h2]
A 19-lesson in-game tutorial: the Welcome card offers a guided tour of the whole mod, or lessons that appear the first time you need them. Replay any lesson from F10 > Guide.

[h2]Multiplayer-friendly[/h2]
Every inventory action goes through the game's own server-checked path, the same way vanilla does it. A few extras (choose-a-number splits, the pause buttons) are host or single-player only.

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]F10[/b] - settings, themes, key bindings and the guide
[*][b]F9[/b] - the HUD Designer
[*][b]Middle mouse, Tab, R, 1-6[/b] - the wheels
[*][b]B[/b] - Universal Inventory. [b]G[/b] - Smart Stow
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]Install only one copy - not this Workshop version and a manual copy at the same time.
[*]After an update, restart the game once so the new glass effects load.
[*]To start completely fresh, type uiareset in the F3 console. It shows what it would delete; uiareset confirm does it.
[/list]

